gate: build refuses unless the 82 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: Rewrites the decoder shutdown 0x030893c4 in place. Its only
  caller is 0x03089bfa in the stop-and-advance helper 0x03089ad6, whose
  argument stays in r5: 0 when the playback task takes the end-of-track
  event 0xEC, 1 for a user skip or stop. Stock closes the decoder's file
  (0x0308936e: HifiFile close 0x74, waits for the 0x75 ack), then halts
  core 1 (0x0306cb0c), and for codec 0 also parks four hardware blocks
  (resets 0xe/0xf, gates 0x6e/0x7e). The rewrite keeps all of that
  except that it skips the halt when r5 == 0, so after a natural end
  of track the decoder stays resident and running, which is the state
  patches/harness/milestone2.md proved accepts the next 0x65 open. It
  skips the halt only for codec 6 (FLAC), the one decoder that proof
  covers: Rockchip's SDK restarts the decoder core for every file
  (StartBBSystem), and no other decoder has been shown to accept a
  second file without that reset, so every other codec halts and parks
  its blocks exactly as stock does. User skips and stops still halt, and the gate (0022) then falls back
  to the full stock reload. If the next track needs a different decoder
  the stock reset-and-start body asserts the core-1 reset itself before
  copying. The tbb table is gone; the freed tail is filled with nops.
  Bytes: patches/gapless/tools/assemble_v2.py.
